// STM32H723ZG platform description for Renode, adapted from Renode's own
// bundled `platforms/cpus/stm32h7.repl` (the H7-family base also used by
// its `stm32h743.repl`/`stm32h753.repl` overlays).
//
// Deliberately NOT resizing axiSram/sram1/sram2/sram4 (and not removing
// flashBank2/sram3) to exactly match our `memory.x`: the H743/753 the
// base file models has a superset of the real H723ZG's RAM -- bigger
// regions, plus a second flash bank and an sram3 our chip doesn't have
// at all. An oversized backing region is harmless for proving the
// firmware boots and reaches its steady-state executor loop (memory.x
// is what actually constrains where our code/data land; this repl only
// needs to back those same addresses with *some* RAM, which it already
// does). The real sram2 address (0x30040000) also collides with the
// base's sram3 at that same address, so correcting sram2 in place isn't
// a no-op edit -- revisit with size-accurate, collision-free regions if
// a later task needs to observe out-of-bounds behavior or emulate DMA
// into a specific SRAM bank.
using "platforms/cpus/stm32h7.repl"

// The base file only models SPI4 (used by its own reference boards) --
// add SPI1 (this board's SD-card SPI, see wind_meter.rs) at its real
// address, same shape as the base's own spi4 entry.
spi1: SPI.STM32H7_SPI @ {
        sysbus 0x40013000;
        rcc RegistrationPeripheralAlias.SPI1
    }
